<v Chana Joffe-Walt>So let's imagine that happens. Jaleel does well in school, overcomes some of his disabilities, and he doesn't need the disability program anymore. That would obviously be great for every one, except it would also threaten Jaleel's family's livelihood. Because Jaleel's family, like a lot of kids on disability, survives off that check. Here's his mom, Nujima King. She's got two other kids, and she's not working.
<v Chana Joffe-Walt>那么让我们想象一下如果那发生了。杰里尔在学校表现出色，克服了一些残疾，他不再需要残疾项目了。这对每个人来说显然都很棒，但这也威胁到了杰里尔一家的生计。因为杰里尔一家，像很多领残疾补助的孩子一样，靠那张支票生存。这是他的妈妈，努吉玛·金（Nujima King）。她还有另外两个孩子，而且她没有工作。

